  "description": "Pin the benchmark set, predeclared tolerance, and runnable procedure that gate the selector cutover.\n\n## Background\n\nA reconciled capability trait or migrated selector goes public only after a pinned benchmark set passes within a predeclared non-regression tolerance. The set covers the selector families marked profile-scoped for the pilot cutover; the tolerance is declared before any cutover measurement exists. This issue delivers the protocol and the runnable procedure only; baseline measurement is a separate issue.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- [hard] REQ-01: A committed procedure names the pinned benchmarks covering the pilot selector families and states the non-regression tolerance, declared before any cutover measurement.\n- [hard] REQ-02: The procedure executes end to end in benchmark mode on a prepared host, and is reproducible from its committed description alone.",
